Hmm. OK. None of the stack stuff is heap.

Let me reconsider. The description mentions "heap buffer overflow". wmem allocations are heap-backed. The dic_precision OOB read is on a heap buffer (wmem_alloc0_array). That's a heap buffer overflow read.

But wait — actually, there might be an even more serious one. Let me look at `dissect_idn_laser_dictionary` again — the write `(config->dic_precision)[i] = 1`. i goes up to word_count*2 = 510. Buffer 511. OK.

